\"violated\\\",\n   \\\"defect_claim\\\":\\\"asserted\\\",\n   \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\n    \\\"The leader lease still counts voters only, so the same node steps down shortly after; the incorrect verification result is bounded by that interval rather than persisting.\\\",\n    \\\"The defect requires a configuration that has non-voters at all; a cluster of voters only cannot exhibit it, since every replication peer is then a voter and the acknowledgement set equals the voter set.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe slowed the heartbeat, election and lease timers and isolated the leader by transport disconnection, so the observed interval is longer than a default-timer deployment would allow; with the default in-memory timers the verification and the lease check compete.\\\",\n    \\\"No write path is affected: entry commitment uses the commitment map, which contains voters only, so this is a read-verification path rather than a commit-rule path.\\\"\n   ],\n   \\\"limitations\\\":[\n    \\\"Measured on one four-peer in-memory cluster with the repository's own facilities and slowed timers; production timings and transports are not covered.\\\",\n    \\\"The probe issued the verification directly rather than through an application that then serves a read, so the stale-read consequence is inferred from the documented purpose of the API rather than measured end to end.\\\",\n    \\\"A single run; the isolation is transport-level and confirmed by direct AppendEntries attempts recorded in the same event.\\\"\n   ]}\n ]\n}\njson.dump(u,open('update.json','w'),indent=2); print('written')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_18-00-28-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"written\n{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"1bdd60fe5af14a33879d92997922e21b\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2395.7810721670103, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": false, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"s-lease\"}, {\"object\": \"knowledge\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@k-verify-nonvoter-ack\"}, {\"object\": \"interpretations\", \"action\": \"append\", \"target\": \"interpretations[0]\", \"investigation_id\": \"790eb5d64ed94ef5aea4736e6f66381d-question-0\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Recorded the leader-verification question as a witnessed violation bound to experiment 790eb5d64ed94ef5aea4736e6f66381d-experiment (CheckRun 5e092a2b160b4a2f955d48ee6fa06ad9, exit 0): event 22 shows three voters with quorum two, a voter unreachable by direct AppendEntries and a reachable non-voter, and event 23 shows VerifyLeader returning success with no error in under a millisecond while the node still led. The account states the mechanism (verification is registered with every replication peer, and that map includes non-voters while the quorum size counts voters only), adds the lease check as the source of the exposure bound, and lists the counterevidence and limits; a behavior entry records it.\"}"}}
